```http
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### POST /files/
# Expected status: 200
# Expected response:
# {
#   "file_size": 12,
#   "token": "supersecret",
#   "fileb_content_type": "text/plain"
# }

POST {{baseUrl}}/files/
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----FastAPIFormBoundary

------FastAPIFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello World!
------FastAPIFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fileb"; filename="test.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello World!
------FastAPIFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="token"

supersecret
------FastAPIFormBoundary--
```

`file` contains **12 bytes** (`Hello World!`), while `fileb` is an `UploadFile`, so FastAPI can report its `content_type` as `text/plain`.
